      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It takes a massive amount of strength to try to hold things together when everything feels like it's collapsing, and pushing yourself further won't break the weight; it will only add more to your own burden. \"Just being there\" isn't the problem, but if the emotional weight is truly crushing you, the only sane choice is to put down the heavy tool and rest before you fall. Please consider taking a step out of this cycle now, because surviving a burnout is infinitely harder than ever before having the chance to just pause. You deserve a life where you aren't the permanent backer for everyone else's falling apart, so please take this moment to breathe for yourself.",
